<title>INDIA: New soybean crop arrives in western Indian market.</title>
<headline>New soybean crop arrives in western Indian market.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The new season's soybean crop has arrived in Sangli in the western state of Maharashtra and quoted at 13,100-13,250 rupees per tonne, delivered at Pithampur plant near Indore.</p>
<p>Arrivals were 50-60 bags in Sangli market on Tuesday due to rains. They were 60 tonnes on Saturday. Two hundred tonnes of soybean was contracted for 10 September delivery till date for the new season.</p>
<p>For the current season, the price of old soybean (harvested last November and December) was at a record high at 13,200-13,400 rupees in Dewas market. The undertone was strong.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were up 100 rupees per tonne on good demand in the local market. The undertone was strong.</p>
<p>Soymeal prices were down in export trading due to lower demand but prices were up by 100 rupees per tonne in the local market. Soymeal yellow was $286-288 per tonne for current season and was $270-272 per tonne for new season's November-15-December shipment. The undertone was weak. Rapeseed extraction was $121-122 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was 4,150-4,200 rupees FOR Bedibunder and was 4,125-4,150 rupees FOR Bhavnagar.</p>
